<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Montségur</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Montségur is a castle on a rocky peak in the Ariège <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a> of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, in the foothills of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pyrenees">Pyrenees</a>. Rebuilt around 1204 as a Cathar refuge, it became their main stronghold during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albigensian-crusade">Albigensian Crusade</a>. After a siege of some ten months it surrendered in March 1244, and more than 200 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catharism">Cathars</a> who refused to recant were burned. The present ruins are of a later fortress.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/montsegur.jpg" alt="Montségur" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Obra pròpia, cedeixo tots els drets (domini públic) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Montsegur.p%C3%B2g1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
